# BUGS

No PHY bring-up, MST, audio, PSR or HDCP: a transmitter or PHY firmware didn't enable stays dark.
Rates are changed only on a PHY in DisplayPort-only mode, and HBR3 isn't trained: its PHY setting is an open question in the spec (its spread-spectrum writes).
Drive levels above 0 come from the vendor's table, whose base values differ from firmware's on the Orange Pi 6 Plus; no sink here has asked for them.
Only RGB at 8 bits a component and a pixel a clock are sent.
An HPD event's sink is read on the interrupt's thread, which waits for each AUX reply, up to 10 ms each, and for a sink just plugged up to 500 ms more.
That the core clears `INTERRUPT_CAUSE` when it is read is presumed, not documented.
